# Project Governance

Brand: FinGem-AI · Product: DnDGem

Phase 0 is CLOSED. Do not reopen gates without a hard contradiction (stop, document, report).

Phase 1 Technical MVP is **CLOSED** (DND-1.1 → DND-1.8). Do not reopen Phase 1 product/architecture decisions without a hard contradiction.

Phase 2 Public Alpha Readiness is **PASS** — Public Alpha **LIVE** (`0.1.0-alpha.0` / `@alpha`).

**Next phase:** Phase 3 — Adaptive Auto-Layout (`docs/roadmap.md`). Do not begin Phase 3 implementation unless the active sprint explicitly requires it.

## CI policy (DND-2.3+)

- Feature → develop: full **local** quality gate; GitHub CI not required / should not run.
- Develop → master: full **GitHub** CI must run and pass before merge.

## Hard exclusions (until an explicit sprint requires them)

Cursor MUST NOT introduce:

- AI / Gemini / OpenAI / Anthropic / local model runtimes
- Flutter implementation
- Vue / Angular / Svelte implementations
- Deterministic Auto-Layout product implementation (belongs Phase 3)
- cloud services / billing / Stripe
- Layout CI SaaS / team accounts / enterprise functionality
- custom native DnD engine
- npm publication / repository visibility changes unless the active sprint explicitly requires it

unless the active sprint explicitly requires it.

Flutter compatibility may be considered architecturally (types, ADRs), but not implemented until scheduled.

AI is optional and outside the critical path; it follows deterministic Auto-Layout (Phase 4).

Repository remains PRIVATE unless an explicit release decision changes visibility.

Public Alpha installs must use **`@alpha`** (`0.1.0-alpha.0`). Do not document bare / `latest` installs as the supported Alpha path.
